    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87473" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προηγ-ητής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who goes before to show the way, guide,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				1292
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ant.</u>
				990
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				<u>Or.</u>
				41(4).12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>one who conducts the bride's car in her procession,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρεωκόμον καὶ προηγητὴν ἀκολουθεῖν
					τῷ ζεύγει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hyp.
					<u>Lyc.</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
